  "narrative": "No new validation was released and no response deadline is pending. With zero new voluntary validation requests remaining, no validation was requested. I left the accepted conclusions in force and moved the two most informative conditional outcome_006 feature_020 checks, H171 and H178, to active investigation.\n\nThe dominant dataset-specific measured association is outcome_006 with feature_021 absent versus present. Under the registered direction, H107 has signed discovery estimate about +0.802 (95% CI +0.782 to +0.822) and independent validation about +0.811 (CI +0.782 to +0.841). On the raw dependency scale this means the feature_021=0 cell has a more negative outcome_006 score, i.e. stronger measured dependency in this supplied dataset. This is far above the approximate outcome_006 10% scale benchmark of about 0.009. Stratified feature_021 comparisons across binary markers, age bands, and other strata remain large and positive, while tested interactions are generally null or imprecise. This supports a large, reproducible outcome_006-specific measured association that is not robustly modified by the tested contexts. It does not establish causality, mechanism, biological interpretation, leakage, or generalizability.\n\nThe second accepted dataset-specific signal is outcome_006 with feature_020 absent versus present. H111 has signed estimate +0.0595 (95% CI +0.0148 to +0.1043), above the approximate clinical benchmark, so it is accepted in this dataset. Supporting strata H195 within feature_060=0 and H197 within feature_002=1 are also accepted with intervals entirely above the benchmark. However, specificity is only partly resolved. H189 excludes null but its lower bound is below the clinical benchmark; H190, H194, H198, H201, H202, and H203 have clinically positive point estimates but are too imprecise. Formal tested interactions H191, H199, and H204 are imprecise and cross null, so robust effect modification is not supported in those tested contexts. The conditional feature_021 analyses are the remaining key specificity gap, which is why H171 and H178 are now active.\n\nThe negative and failed-validation findings are also scientifically important. Promising discovery effects were not robust under validation or clinical-scale assessment: H19, H23, H62, H57/H64, H72/H74, H94/H95, and H154 did not replicate with clinically meaningful intervals. Broad comparisons involving feature_060, feature_002, feature_047, feature_023, feature_034, feature_037, and many categorical predictors were mostly null, too small, or too imprecise. The accepted findings are therefore concentrated on outcome_006 and are dataset-specific measured associations, not a general predictor map.\n\nMost informative next work, using only within-data analyses because validation is exhausted, is to resolve the feature_020 conditional marker structure, especially H171 and H178 and related joint marker context, and to assess whether any feature_020 signal persists after accounting for the large feature_021 association. Further validation would be most valuable for H111 and any conditional feature_020 finding, but no causal, mechanistic, leakage, or generalizability conclusions are justified at this stage.",
  "research_notes": "FINAL SCIENTIFIC REPORT (iteration 16; no validation budget remaining). The accepted dataset-specific signal set is dominated by outcome_006 feature_021: H107 discovery R118 and validation R121 show an extremely large positive signed absent-versus-present effect, about +0.80 in both analyses, far above the approximate 10% outcome_006 benchmark around 0.009. The accepted subgroup/stratum claims for feature_021, including H129, H130, H132, H133, H135, H136, H137, H138, H143, H144, H149, H163, H164, H170, and H176, show consistent near-magnitude effects across tested binary-marker and age contexts; the formal interactions that were tested, such as H131, H134, H150, and H165, do not provide robust evidence of effect modification. Cross-outcome feature_021 tests mostly rejected, and H154 outcome_005 failed validation, so the association is best described as a very strong outcome_006-specific measured association in this dataset, not a causal or broadly generalizable dependency-marker relationship.\n\nA second accepted outcome_006 signal is feature_020 absent versus present: H111 discovery R157 gives signed +0.0595 (95% CI +0.0148 to +0.1043), clinically positive by the approximate outcome_006 benchmark. H195 within feature_060=0 and H197 within feature_002=1 are accepted robust strata because their intervals lie entirely above the benchmark. The specificity picture is incomplete: H189 is null-excluding but not wholly above benchmark; H190, H194, H198, H201, H202, and H203 are unresolved because they are imprecise or only partially above threshold; H191, H199, and H204 do not support robust tested modification. The most important remaining specificity question is whether feature_020 is independent of feature_021 or attenuated by joint marker structure. Therefore H171 and H178 were moved to active investigation; they test feature_020 conditional on feature_021 present/absent states. The next analysis should prioritize these conditional feature_020 claims and any related marker-context checks, especially around feature_021, feature_047/feature_064 ambiguity, and the untested or unresolved age and interaction claims.\n\nNegative findings are broad and important: feature_060, feature_002, feature_047, feature_023, feature_034, feature_037, feature_055, and many categorical predictors failed to show clinically meaningful, robust effects. Several discovery effects were refuted or narrowed by validation: H19, H23, H62, H57/H64, H72/H74, H94/H95, and H154. Many other near-threshold discovery effects remained unresolved because intervals were too wide or not entirely above the clinical benchmark. Overall scientific conclusion: in this supplied dataset, the scientifically meaningful measured associations are concentrated in outcome_006, with a validated, very large feature_021 association and a smaller but clinically positive accepted feature_020 association whose marker-specificity is not fully resolved. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations; causality, mechanism, leakage, and generalizability remain unresolved."
