  "research_notes": "FINAL SCIENTIFIC REPORT (iteration 18 synthesis)\n\nEvidence status: No new validation was released, no assessments were due, and voluntary independent validation is exhausted. The synthesis uses existing discovery and prior validation in the supplied ledger.\n\nSupported findings: The dominant within-dataset measured association is outcome_006 with feature_021 absent versus present. Under H107 (feature_021=0 versus 1, direction -1), signed discovery difference is +0.802 (95% CI +0.782 to +0.822), independent validation +0.811 (CI +0.782 to +0.841). On raw scale this means feature_021=0 has much more negative outcome_006, i.e. stronger measured dependency. The effect is orders above the outcome_006 approximate clinical benchmark of 10% of absolute mean (~0.0093). It is also robust across many marker strata (feature_034, feature_047, feature_060, feature_002, feature_020, age/feature_061 bands, feature_039 bands), and tested interactions do not establish heterogeneity.\n\nA second supported association is outcome_006 with feature_020 absent versus present: H111 signed +0.0595 (95% CI +0.0148 to +0.1043), above benchmark but not independently validated. Feature_020 is also robust in two prespecified marker strata: H197 within feature_002=1 (+0.0853, CI +0.0215 to +0.1492) and H195 within feature_060=0 (+0.0881, CI +0.0214 to +0.1548). Other feature_020 strata are supportive but not fully clinically robust because lower bounds are near zero or below the benchmark (e.g. H171, H178, H189, H206, H208, H216, H203).\n\nNegative/null findings: Many predictors show no clinically meaningful measured differences on the outcome examined, including feature_060, feature_002, feature_047, feature_023, feature_034, feature_037, feature_012, feature_050, feature_045, feature_042, feature_028, feature_063, feature_055, feature_064, feature_019, feature_022, and feature_048 in various outcome comparisons. Broad outcome_006 screens H219-H222 remain inconclusive or below robust standards. H221 rejects the registered positive feature_028 level_002 versus level_003 association on outcome_008. H223 and H224 reject robust positive feature_034 and feature_045 effect modification of feature_020 within feature_021=0, although H224 shows a negative signed interaction pattern suggestive of attenuation. Several isolated discovery signals failed independent validation or clinical threshold, including examples H19, H23, H57/H64, H62, H72, H74/H83, H94/H95, and H154.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty: Feature_020 specificity is incomplete; its overall and some marker-stratum signals are robust, but conditional strata are imprecise and no interaction has been robustly established. The possibility of attenuation by feature_045, feature_047, feature_060, or feature_002 remains open. Broad screens for feature_022, feature_019, feature_048, and feature_028 have not reached clinically robust evidence after accounting for multiplicity. Because many subgroup/interaction tests were made, borderline lower-bound effects are not treated as supported. Independent validation for feature_020 was not possible because validation budget is exhausted.\n\nMost informative next analysis: Focus on the feature_020 association after removing the dominant feature_021 signal. Analyze already registered H225/H226 (feature_020 within feature_021=0 split by feature_045), H227/H228 (feature_022 and feature_019 within feature_021=0), H229 (feature_020 within feature_021=0, feature_002=1, feature_060=0), and newly registered feature_020 tests by feature_060 and feature_002 combinations within feature_021=0. A result will be accepted only if the full signed interval exceeds the outcome-specific 10%-of-mean benchmark with adequate cells; otherwise it remains supportive but not accepted.\n\nInterpretation limits: These are dataset-specific measured associations among opaque measured predictors and CRISPR dependency outcomes. No causal, mechanistic, leakage, or external-generalizability conclusion is drawn. Opaque levels are nominal; signs follow signed hypothesis conventions."
