  "narrative": "Assessment follows the signed-direction convention: for a direction -1 claim, a positive signed estimate means the exposed condition is associated with a more negative dependency score, whereas for a direction +1 claim, a positive signed estimate means the exposed condition is less negative than the comparator. I used the conservative supplied-data benchmark of approximately 10% of the absolute outcome mean, about 0.0093 for outcome_006 and outcome_014, and required the full signed lower bound to exceed that benchmark before accepting a discovery-only or subgroup association. The strongest new accepted result is H275: within feature_007 present, feature_021 absent versus present gives signed +0.7635, 95% CI +0.7137 to +0.8132, cell sizes 157/49. This is a very large, clinically meaningful and statistically robust dataset-specific association, and it shows that the dominant feature_021 signal is not eliminated in the rare feature_007 present subgroup. H276 is also accepted: in the feature_021 absent majority, feature_006 present versus absent on outcome_014 gives signed +0.0773, CI +0.0163 to +0.1384, with lower bound well above the outcome_014 benchmark; this strengthens the already accepted outcome-specific H254 association. H280 is accepted more cautiously because it is the secondary feature_020 candidate localized in the feature_007 absent majority: signed +0.0579, CI +0.0101 to +0.1058, cell sizes 1497/297. Its lower bound just exceeds the benchmark, so it supports H111 but remains a discovery-only, multiplicity-sensitive association. By contrast, H273 tests feature_007 within feature_021 present and gives a small opposite signed estimate, -0.0050, CI -0.0505 to +0.0405; together with the overall H268 lower bound below the clinical benchmark and the H274 interaction null/opposite result, I reject H268 and its robustness tests as not established as scientifically meaningful. H274 is not accepted as a positive feature_007 interaction with feature_021 present: the signed estimate is negative, -0.0428, and the interval includes zero, with no clinically meaningful positive lower bound. H277 remains unresolved and deferred: feature_006 on outcome_014 within feature_021 present gives a clinically sized positive signed estimate, +0.0272, but the interval is very wide and includes zero, so the rare subgroup does not establish the effect. H278 is unresolved and deferred as a possible modification of the feature_006 association by feature_021, but the claimed direction is not supported: the interaction estimate is -0.0501 with a wide interval including zero. H279 remains unresolved and deferred because the feature_020 contrast within feature_007 present is clinically sized, +0.0540, but the rare comparator gives a very wide interval crossing zero. Among the four additional screened binary comparisons, H113, H125, and H147 are rejected as unsupported or clinically trivial: H113 and H125 are small and opposite to their registered positive-direction claims, and H147 is far below the benchmark despite wide uncertainty. H148 remains unresolved and deferred because feature_046 has a clinically sized positive signed estimate, +0.0399, but the interval includes zero and extends below the benchmark, leaving only low-confidence signal. No independent validation can be requested because voluntary validation capacity is exhausted. All accepted statements remain observational associations in this supplied dataset with opaque predictor labels; they do not establish causality, mechanism, leakage-free biological interpretation, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated final-phase notes. Supported dataset-specific CRISPR-dependency associations are: (1) H107, outcome_006 feature_021 absent versus present, replicated large association, discovery signed +0.8019 CI +0.7823 to +0.8216 and validation signed +0.8115 CI +0.7821 to +0.8408; (2) H275, the same feature_021 absent-versus-present signal within feature_007 present, discovery signed +0.7635 CI +0.7137 to +0.8132; (3) H111, outcome_006 feature_020 absent versus present, discovery-only signed +0.0595 CI +0.0148 to +0.1043; (4) H280, feature_020 within feature_007 absent, discovery-only signed +0.0579 CI +0.0101 to +0.1058, supporting H111 but not independent; (5) H254, outcome_014 feature_006 present versus absent, discovery-only signed +0.0647 CI +0.0108 to +0.1186; and (6) H276, the same feature_006 association within feature_021 absent, discovery-only signed +0.0773 CI +0.0163 to +0.1384. Negative or rejected results now include H273 and H274, which do not support a clinically meaningful feature_007 effect robust to feature_021, and H268 is rejected as not clinically meaningful/robust despite a marginally positive full-population estimate. Additional rejected screened binary predictors include H113, H125, and H147. Unresolved low-confidence candidates are H277, H278, H279, H148, and previously retained rare or wide-interval candidates such as feature_023 on outcome_006 and rare feature_028 level contrasts. New proposals focus robustness on the accepted/secondary signals: feature_021 within feature_007 absent, feature_007 within feature_021 absent, and feature_020 interaction by feature_007. Validation capacity is exhausted. All conclusions remain supplied-data observational associations, not causal, mechanistic, leakage-free, or generalizable claims."
