  "narrative": "FINAL SCIENTIFIC REPORT.\n\nNo new independent validation was released in this synthesis, and voluntary validation capacity is exhausted. The conclusions below are dataset-specific observational associations with opaque predictor labels; they do not establish causality, mechanism, leakage-free biology, or external generalizability.\n\nSUPPORTED FINDINGS.\nH107 is the principal supported finding. For outcome_006, feature_021 absent versus present under direction -1 gives a signed discovery estimate of +0.8019 with 95% CI +0.7823 to +0.8216, R118, and independent validation +0.8115 with validation CI +0.7821 to +0.8408 under the stricter multiplicity-adjusted alpha, R121. Because returned estimates are already signed and more negative dependency scores mean stronger dependency, this indicates that feature_021 absence is associated with a much stronger outcome_006 dependency than feature_021 presence. The effect is far above the conservative clinical benchmark of roughly 0.0093 for outcome_006 and is replicated independently.\nH275 shows that the same feature_021 absent-versus-present signal persists in the rare feature_007-present subgroup: signed +0.7635, CI +0.7137 to +0.8132, R266.\nH111 and H280 are secondary supported but unvalidated associations for outcome_006: feature_020 absent versus present gives signed +0.0595, CI +0.0148 to +0.1043, R157, and within feature_007 absent gives signed +0.0579, CI +0.0101 to +0.1058, R271. These are clinically sized relative to outcome_006, but they remain discovery-only, multiplicity-sensitive, and dependent on the possibility that the feature_020 and feature_021 predictors encode overlapping structure.\nH254 and H276 support an outcome_014 association for feature_006 presence: full-population signed +0.0647, CI +0.0108 to +0.1186, R237, and within feature_021 absent signed +0.0773, CI +0.0163 to +0.1384, R267. Under direction -1, positive signed estimates mean feature_006-present scores are more negative, i.e., stronger dependency. This is also discovery-only and has not been independently validated.\n\nNEGATIVE AND REJECTED RESULTS.\nI reassessed H282 and reject it. Within feature_021 absent, feature_007 present versus absent under direction +1 gives signed +0.0378, CI +0.0081 to +0.0675, R231. The interval is above zero, but its lower bound is below the clinical benchmark, so the evidence does not establish a scientifically meaningful feature_007 association in this subgroup. This is consistent with rejecting H268, H273, and H274, and feature_007 should not be presented as a robust clinically meaningful predictor. H281 and H283 are closed as unresolved because no usable evidence became available.\nRejected or unsupported results dominate the broader search. These include validated or repeated below-benchmark, null, or opposite findings such as H19, H23, H37, H39, H42, H57/H64, H62, H72, H74/H83, H94/H95, and H154, as well as numerous screened binary or categorical contrasts that are small, imprecise, opposite to the registered direction, or below the clinical benchmark. Negative results here mean that the supplied dataset does not support scientifically meaningful differences at the chosen threshold; they do not prove absence of effects in the broader world.\n\nUNRESOLVED UNCERTAINTY.\nSeveral candidates remain unresolved and should not be treated as established findings. H277 and H278 leave outcome_014 feature_006 within the rare feature_021-present setting uncertain and imprecise. H279 leaves feature_020 within feature_007-present uncertain because the interval is wide. H148 and H128 leave feature_046 and feature_023 as low-confidence outcome_006 candidates. Rare predictor contrasts, including some feature_028 level contrasts and other rare subgroup estimates, remain unresolved because cells are small and intervals are wide. Multiplicity from broad screening further lowers confidence in any single unresolved candidate.\n\nMOST INFORMATIVE NEXT ANALYSIS.\nThe highest-value next step is strict pre-specified external or fully held-out validation with no further post-hoc mining. Primary endpoint: outcome_006, feature_021 absent versus present. Secondary endpoints: outcome_006 feature_020 absent versus present and outcome_014 feature_006 present versus absent. Pre-specify a small set of effect-modification checks by feature_021 and feature_007 for the secondary candidates, using multiplicity-adjusted intervals and requiring clinically meaningful lower bounds. If internal analysis continues, restrict it to targeted robustness of H107 and the few secondary associations rather than broad new screening. All final claims remain limited to observational associations in the supplied dataset."
}

